    <values>
        <field>Body__c</field>
        <value xsi:type="xsd:string">A Black Nova Scotian businesswoman who refused to leave the whites-only section of a New Glasgow movie theatre in 1946. She was dragged out, jailed overnight, and convicted of avoiding a one-cent tax. In 2010 Nova Scotia granted her a free pardon and apologized. In 2018 she became the first Canadian woman shown on a regular Canadian banknote, the ten-dollar bill.</value>
